          deck: 'Standard Austrian 54-card Tarock pack: 22 trumps (Tarocks), 8 cards each in four suits.',
          equipment: '',
          dealing: "Dealer shuffles, player to left cuts. Deal 12 cards to each player in batches of 6, anticlockwise, starting with player to dealer's right. Place two packets of 3 cards face down in middle as talon.",
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Win tricks containing valuable cards. In positive contracts, need 36+ of 71 card points. Various contracts have different objectives.',
          gameplay: "Dealer deals 12 cards each and 6 to the talon. Players bid (Sechserdreier, Rufer mit Spatz/Uhu, Dreier) or say Erster; if all pass, Fahren is played. Bidder calls a King (in Rufer) or takes 3 or 6 talon cards and discards. Announcements and Kontras follow. Player to dealer's right leads; 12 tricks, follow suit, must trump if unable to follow. Highest trump wins trick, else highest of led suit. Team with 36+ of 71 card points wins the game; bonuses and game points are settled in cash.",
          keyRules: [
            'Deal 12 cards each and 6 to the talon in two packets of 3; deal and play anticlockwise.',
            'Bid Sechserdreier, Rufer mit Spatz/Uhu, or Dreier, or say Erster; if all pass, Fahren is played.',
            'In Rufer, call a King for partner; bidder takes 3 talon cards (or 6 in Sechserdreier) and discards; 5-point cards and most trumps cannot be discarded.',
            "Follow suit; must trump if unable to follow. Highest Tarock wins trick, else highest of led suit. Player to dealer's right leads.",
            '36+ of 71 card points wins the game; game points and bonuses (Trull, Four Kings, Pagat Ultimo, Uhu, King Ultimo, Valat) settled in cash.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'In positive contracts, aim for 36+ points. The 5-point cards (SkÃ¼s, XXI, I, Kings) are crucial - there are only 8 of them totaling 40 points. Queens (4 pts) and Knights (3 pts) are also valuable.',
          intermediate: 'Talon selection: Look for packets with kings or high trumps. In Rufer, if the called king is in the talon, you play alone - consider this risk when calling. In Fahren, try to take as few points as possible - even taking zero points is a valid strategy.',
          advanced: 'Announcement timing: Announcing Pagat Ultimo or Uhu doubles their value but commits you to a specific play. Only announce if you have strong position in trumps. In Sechserdreier, with all 6 talon cards, you have perfect information - use this advantage. The risk/reward (+2/-4) means you need a strong hand to bid Sechserdreier.',
          tips: [
            'Track the 22 trumps carefully - knowing which high trumps remain is essential.',
            'In Rufer mit Spatz/Uhu, the announced bonus can be won/lost independently of the game.',
            'Fahren is dangerous if you have many high cards - sometimes bidding a weak Rufer is safer.',
            "The Uhu (trump II) is easier to make than Pagat Ultimo as it's played earlier.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
